# /etc/cerber-alert.env - Cerber alert channel configuration
#
# Deploy path: /etc/cerber-alert.env (mode 0640, owned by root)
# Every cerber-*.service unit has `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/cerber-alert.env`
# so a single file drives R9, R11, R12, R13, R14, R15, mesh, edge-ingest,
# fleet-HA, and any future rule.
#
# Historical note (2026-08-29): audit found this file only ever contained
# CERBER_ALERT_EMAIL on rope-vps-lon1, so every page since 2026-07-29 has
# been silently no-op'd with the journal line:
#
#     [cerber-*] page skipped: SMTP not configured (set EMAIL_* in
#     /etc/cerber-alert.env); recipient would be contact@onguene.com
#
# The classifier still writes /var/lib/datachain-rope/cerber/*.ndjson audit
# trails and still tarpits malicious IPs regardless of email status; the
# email channel is purely operator-visibility. This file is the canonical
# template for turning that channel on.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CORE (already set on prod, keep unchanged)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CERBER_ALERT_EMAIL=contact@onguene.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANNEL A (recommended): SendGrid HTTP v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# page-email.mjs auto-detects SendGrid when EMAIL_HOST contains "sendgrid"
# OR EMAIL_PASS starts with "SG.". No STARTTLS handshake, no port 25/587
# egress needed. Set the two vars below with a real SendGrid API key and
# every cerber rule starts paging within its next tick.
#
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.sendgrid.net
# EMAIL_PASS=SG.your-real-sendgrid-api-key-here
# EMAIL_FROM=cerber@datachain.network

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANNEL B (alternative): raw STARTTLS SMTP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# For self-hosted or non-SendGrid providers. page-email.mjs uses node:tls
# directly (no msmtp / no external SMTP client needed).
#
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.your-provider.com
# EMAIL_PORT=587
# EMAIL_USER=cerber@datachain.network
# EMAIL_PASS=your-smtp-password
# EMAIL_FROM=cerber@datachain.network

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: alert-cooldown tuning
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cerber deduplicates identical pages within this window to avoid flooding.
# Default is 6h; lower it if you want faster re-notification after a
# transient recovery.
#
# CERBER_ALERT_COOLDOWN_MS=21600000
